From 27b1aaac2fc4fc0b7cc9cad47b8aa7ff2829f440 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 18:55:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm: nexell: self-program DPC timing + HDMI PHY (own modeset)

The driver now programmes the display pipeline itself instead of riding on the
mode the bootloader set for its boot logo: it sets the DPC video timing and
the HDMI PHY/Link preset for the requested mode, so it works independently of
u-boot and supports the modes the HDMI presets provide (480p/576p/720p/1080p
etc.), intersected with the monitor EDID.

Integrates the vendor SoC layer, decoupled from the 4.14 KMS glue via a small
SoC-only header (s5pxx18_soc_dp_glue.h) replacing s5pxx18_drm_dp.h: dp_dev
(nx_soc_dp_cont_* control + plane), soc_dpc (DPC timing), dp_hdmi + hdmi_presets
(HDMI Link/Core + PHY presets), soc_disptop(_clk), reg_hdmi. The KMS driver
constructs an nx_drm_device, maps the DPC/MLC/HDMI bases + HDMI resets, and on
each modeset runs: nx_dp_hdmi_mode_set -> nx_soc_dp_cont_prepare (DPC) ->
nx_dp_hdmi_mode_commit (PHY) -> power. mode_valid now accepts any preset-backed
mode; if setup fails it falls back to the bootloader mode.

HW-verified on a NanoPi Fire3: 'set hdmi mode to vic4,1280x720@60Hz',
'HDMI: PHY [Ready Done]', console renders correctly from the self-programmed
pipeline; modetest lists 720p/480p/640x480.

Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
